    "summaries": [
      {
        "action_date": "2025-01-23",
        "action_desc": "Introduced in House",
        "text": "<p><strong>Jobs Now Act of 2025</strong></p><p>This bill directs the Department of Labor to conduct a two-year pilot program to award grants to general local governmental units or community-based organizations to retain, employ, or train individuals for positions that provide a public service. At least 50% of grant funds must be used to retain employees who would otherwise be laid off due to budget cuts.</p><p>Labor must encourage grantees to use grant funds to retain, employ, or train veterans, individuals with disabilities, individuals receiving unemployment benefits, or dislocated workers.</p>",
        "update_date": "2026-02-25T12:47:43Z"
      }
    ]
